EODHD × Notion Integration
Pulsn pulls live market data from EODHD and writes it directly into your Notion database properties — automatically, at a frequency determined by your plan.
Free forever for 1 database · No EODHD account needed
What this integration does
Reads from EODHD
Pulsn fetches live market data from EODHD's API — price, 24h change, and volume — for any stock, ETF, fund, or forex pair you configure.
Writes into Notion
The values are written directly into your Notion database's Number properties, exactly as you've mapped them.
Runs automatically
You configure it once. Pulsn handles the scheduling, polling, and updating from that point on — no action needed from you.
Supported EODHD metrics
Each metric maps to a separate Notion Number property.
| Metric | Asset types | Notes | 
|---|---|---|
| Current price | Stocks, ETFs, funds, forex | |
| 24h price change (%) | Stocks, ETFs, funds | Positive or negative percentage | 
| 24h trading volume | Stocks, ETFs, funds | 
How to connect EODHD to Notion
Authorize Pulsn
Connect Pulsn to your Notion workspace via the official OAuth flow. Select the database you want to keep updated.
Configure an EODHD sync flow
Choose EODHD, search for a ticker (e.g. AAPL, VOO, EUR/USD), pick a metric (e.g. Price), and map it to a Notion property.
Done — it runs itself
Pulsn syncs the data on your schedule. No API keys, no code, no cron jobs needed.
Why use Pulsn instead of the EODHD API directly?
No coding required
Using the raw EODHD API requires writing and hosting code. Pulsn does all of that for you.
Writes directly to Notion
The API gives you data. Turning that into Notion property updates requires building a second integration. Pulsn handles both sides.
Automatic scheduling
You'd need a cron job or scheduler to run your API calls on a schedule. Pulsn manages this for you.
Free tier available
Start at no cost. Upgrade only when you need more databases or faster sync frequencies.
Frequently asked questions
Do I need an EODHD API key?
No. Pulsn handles the EODHD API connection on your behalf — you don't need to create an account with EODHD or manage any API keys.
How often is EODHD data updated in Notion?
Pulsn syncs based on your plan: every 24 hours on the free plan, every hour on Growth, and every 15 minutes on Power.
Which EODHD metrics are supported?
Current price, 24h change, and 24h trading volume. More metrics are planned.
Which asset types does EODHD support?
EODHD covers stocks (US and international), ETFs, mutual funds, and forex pairs. If a ticker is listed on EODHD, Pulsn can sync it.
Does Pulsn use the official EODHD API?
Yes. Pulsn pulls data from EODHD's official API, ensuring reliable and accurate market data for your Notion databases.
